  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1102 PM CDT Sun Jun 14 2026\n\nThe upper level flow will become conducive to shortwaves passing \nthrough, so Wednesday onward will have more rain chances and \npossibly more strong to severe storms. Wednesday night into Thursday \nmorning, chances for rain will increase from a front approaching our \narea that will pass through Friday. Rain chances will peak Thursday \nnight into Friday morning, and slowly taper from there. Guidance is \nshowing that the chances for severe weather with this front are low, \nbut we will continue to assess as the shorter range models get a \nhold of it. Temperatures will continue to warm into the upper 80s to \nlow 90s by Thursday, and then the next cold front swings through \ndropping things back down to the upper 70s and low 80s.",
